logs/

# Data files
*.mmdb
data/*.mmdb
data/api_keys.json
# data/phone_reports.db holds ingested FTC Do Not Call complaints. Public domain, but it
# is derived operator data measured in hundreds of MB after a full backfill, and it is
# rebuilt by scripts/ingest_ftc_dnc.py rather than distributed.
data/phone_reports.db
data/phone_reports.db-journal
data/phone_reports.db-wal
# data/yara/ holds operator-fetched detection rules under their own licences.
data/yara/

# Security files (IMPORTANT: never commit keys or secrets)
*.key
*.pem
secrets/

# Personal AI workflow instructions (never commit)
CLAUDE.md

# Tailwind standalone CLI binary (46MB; download on demand, see tailwind.config.js)
# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored "tools/" also matched app/tools/, the
# identity scan's subprocess worker package, and silently kept it out of git.
/tools/

# Agent scratch: worktrees and subagent-driven-development ledgers/briefs/reviews
.worktrees/
.superpowers/

# Runtime analysis artifacts (bind-mounted in Docker; never committed).
# data/analyses/ holds e-mail findings: sender addresses, subjects, Received-chain IPs.
data/scans/
data/screenshots/
data/analyses/
# data/submissions/ holds proposed abuse.ch submissions (indicators, analyst names,
# operator decisions). data/quarantine/ holds live malware samples awaiting approval.
data/submissions/
data/quarantine/
# data/activity/ is the request log. It records client IPs, countries and the paths
# that were looked up, so it carries the same sensitivity as the analysis records.
data/activity/
# data/identity/ holds account-enumeration results and infostealer exposure findings
# about named individuals. Never committed.
data/identity/

# --- Internal-only: not meant for the public repo. Added after the
# .github/workflows/sync-public.yml workflow that used to enforce this split
# was deleted (2026-07-30), so pushes stopped being filtered. ---
ENHANCEMENT_PLAN.md
nexus_auto_update.sh
scripts/cloudflare_admin.py
docs/operations.md
docs/cloudflare-admin.md
docs/dev-notes.md
# Agent scratch (briefs, diffs, review notes) stays ignored, but design specs are
# decision records, so they are tracked. See tasks/lessons.md (2026-07-28, "Agent
# scratch directories swallow the audit trail").
#
# The glob is `docs/superpowers/*`, not `docs/superpowers/`: git cannot re-include
# anything beneath an excluded directory, so the directory itself has to stay
# traversable for the negation below to take effect.
docs/superpowers/*
!docs/superpowers/specs/
cleanup-step1-untrack.sh
cleanup-step2-history-rewrite.sh
